    "created_at": "2023-03-21T13:14:38Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-03-21T13:32:57Z",
    "body": "Turns out that [the intent of `:open`](https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/7319#issuecomment-1242377579) is not just to match open popovers, but also other kinds of openness, such as `<details open>` (thanks @bkardell for sending me the resolution). So `element.matches(':open')` isn't an effective way to detect if the element is an open popover.\r\n\r\nThere are even cases where a single element, such as `<details popover>`, can be two kinds of `:open` at the same time.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
